  "body": "What happens: in one lathe setup, two threading operations (default parameters), both generated and Ok. Save the project, load it into a fresh world: the first op (TH0) reads Ok, the second (TH1) reads Stale with reason \"operation 'TH0' ahead of it in the program changed - regenerate the program in order\" (`rest.rs`, `prior_stale`). Reproduced on origin/main 64506ff5.\n\nExpected: a project that was all Ok when saved loads all Ok (the #169 law: save and load do not stale an op).\n\nCause (traced, not fixed): TH1's stamp digests TH0's cached path through `Toolpath::path_sig` (`crates/app/src/path_sig.rs`, bit-exact hash of every move field), stored when the cache is built. The generated TH0 path carries `y = 6.050000000000001`; the project file writes moves through the lattice snap (`MoveDto`, `cl::lattice`) and the loaded cache has `y = 6.05`. Same 28 moves, first differing move is index 0, so the loaded `path_sig` differs (6467650602549402493 vs 17772775613656745229 for TH1's own, TH0 likewise) and TH1's stored rest digest no longer matches. Any op whose generated coordinates are off the lattice, followed by a dependent op in the same chain, would go Stale the same way; threading is where it shows (the first op of a chain is unaffected as it digests no predecessor).\n\nReproduction (scratch test, a copy of `crates/app/tests/turning_thread.rs` with its helpers `thread_world`, `create`, `thread_params`, `status`, plus):\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn probe_two_threading_ops_reload() {\n    let (world, mut history) = thread_world();\n    create(&world, &mut history, \"TH0\", \"TD-1732-60\", thread_params());\n    create(&world, &mut history, \"TH1\", \"TD-1732-60\", thread_params());\n    assert_eq!(status(&world, \"TH0\"), OpStatus::Ok);\n    assert_eq!(status(&world, \"TH1\"), OpStatus::Ok);\n    let b = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"probe-stale-{}.json\", std::process::id()));\n    camcraft_app::project::save(&world, &b).expect(\"saved\");\n    let other = new_world();\n    camcraft_app::project::load(&other, &b).expect(\"loaded\");\n    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&b);\n    for n in [\"TH0\", \"TH1\"] {\n        assert_eq!(status(&other, n), OpStatus::Ok, \"{n}\"); // TH1: left Stale, right Ok\n    }\n}\n```\n\nLikely fixes to weigh: compute `path_sig` over the snapped moves at generation (so the stored cache equals what a load gives), or snap the generated path when the cache is built. Either must keep save-load-save byte identity.\n\nFound while refreshing #517 / #468 / #518 (the thread infeed stack): its test `the_plan_rides_the_project_file_and_a_default_one_is_absent` fails on this, and on main the same defect exists without that stack.\n\nDone means: the probe above passes (both ops Ok after load), pinned in the turning_thread suite, and the project-file roundtrip suites stay green.\n",
